            <ArticleTitle>Beta-blocker therapy can mask ECG signs of pericarditis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>413-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>PR-segment changes of ECG can help differentiate acute myocardial infarct from pericarditis preventing the patient from an unnecessary coronarography. Here we present a case where beta-blocker therapy masked PR-segment changes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
